{"case_id":"C006","gap_exists":true,"gap_type":["API protocol","state","input semantics"],"confidence":98,"affected_functions":["decoder.decode_sos","decoder.restart_frame!","fuzz_image_decoder"],"reason":"H0 does not exercise the decoder lifecycle implicated by S1. It never calls decoder.restart_frame!, so it cannot test whether restart_frame! correctly clears bitstream_is_closed before a repeated decode. It also treats any non-OK decode_frame result as terminal and does not vary or resume the source-closure state, leaving decode_sos behavior around args.src.is_closed(), $short read, synthetic zero padding, and bitstream_is_closed transitions materially uncovered.","evidence":["S1 adds decoder.bitstream_is_closed and branches in decoder.decode_sos on args.src.is_closed() and not this.bitstream_is_closed.","That branch appends 264 zero bytes, advances bitstream_wi, and sets bitstream_is_closed=true, creating closure-dependent state behavior.","S1 changes decoder.restart_frame! to set this.bitstream_is_closed=false, directly implicating repeated-frame/restart lifecycle testing.","fuzz_image_decoder only calls decode_image_config, decode_frame_config, and decode_frame; it never calls restart_frame!.","After decode_frame returns a non-OK status, fuzz_image_decoder immediately goes to exit, including for $short read, so it does not resume decoding after changing input availability or closure."],"recommended_action":"Add a lifecycle/streaming harness path that supplies JPEG data incrementally, exercises both open and closed io_reader states, resumes after $short read, completes a decode, calls restart_frame!(0, an exercised io_position), and decodes again to cover bitstream_is_closed set/reset behavior."}
